  "title": "Arecibo Observatory",
  "summary": "The Arecibo Observatory in Puerto Rico centred on a 1,000-foot (305 m) fixed radio/radar telescope built in a natural sinkhole from 1960 to 1963. It was the world's largest single-aperture radio telescope until 2016. Cable failures made its 900-ton platform fall onto the dish on 1 December 2020.",
